(6571972, 979398, 10785, '<td valign="top">Cute toddler picture. Tbe focus seems to be either a little in front of or a little behind the eyes. But those eyes are huge, almond color and beautiful. I think the color overall is a little cool and could use a little warming up with a white balance adjustment.</td>', 'Cute toddler picture. Tbe focus seems to be either a little in front of or a little behind the eyes. But those eyes are huge, almond color and beautiful. I think the color overall is a little cool and could use a little warming up with a white balance adjustment.', '2011-10-19 21:44:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(6571973, 979278, 10785, '<td valign="top">Definitely a cutie and a natural model! Great Pose! The lighting is nice and even. Great catch lights in the eyes. The picture could be a tad sharper and a tad brighter overall. But otherwise excellent!</td>', 'Definitely a cutie and a natural model! Great Pose! The lighting is nice and even. Great catch lights in the eyes. The picture could be a tad sharper and a tad brighter overall. But otherwise excellent!', '2011-10-19 21:45:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(6571974, 979407, 10785, '<td valign="top">The general rule of photography is to get close to the subject. I think this is a little too close. The sippy cup is giant and takes up too much of the picture and takes focus away from your subject. The eyes are definitely focused well and you got good catchlights.</td>', 'The general rule of photography is to get close to the subject. I think this is a little too close. The sippy cup is giant and takes up too much of the picture and takes focus away from your subject. The eyes are definitely focused well and you got good catchlights.', '2011-10-19 21:48:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(6571977, 979456, 10785, '<td valign="top">Very cute expression. I think the exposure needs to be brightened up a bit. Either a touch more shutter or a bigger aperture to let in more light. Maybe one stop more. Good focus but a bit sharper in the final processing to bring out the textures.</td>', 'Very cute expression. I think the exposure needs to be brightened up a bit. Either a touch more shutter or a bigger aperture to let in more light. Maybe one stop more. Good focus but a bit sharper in the final processing to bring out the textures.', '2011-10-19 21:49:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(6571979, 978636, 10785, '<td valign="top">Hey... Rembrandt lighting!!</td>', 'Hey... Rembrandt lighting!!', '2011-10-19 21:50:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(6572011, 979402, 104230, '<td valign="top">This is just precious! Wonderful in so many ways, the pose, the outfit, that cherubic mouth, the set up, the textures, the background. Thanks for this wonderful image.</td>', 'This is just precious! Wonderful in so many ways, the pose, the outfit, that cherubic mouth, the set up, the textures, the background. Thanks for this wonderful image.', '2011-10-19 23:00:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(6572020, 979250, 124815, '<td valign="top">Very, very ambitious shot. Hard to mark though. I applaud your work, tenacity, humour, fearlessness, photo skills.<br/>Am wondering what Vermeer would think of it.<br/>Do you know the work of Ori Gerscht?<br/> <br/>Since I have an inkling of the photographer I can formulate several problems that I have with this picture: <u>you wanted to tell too much</u> and crowded your shot with too many props, the opposite of what Vermeer did. <br/>Hard to crop it but it might benefit from it. <br/>The screen looks a bit cheap and does not match the intention and the style of the foreground. Same for the chair, an almost Adirondack style as far from the subject as it could be. The window in the background should have been obstructed in favor of the central subject.<br/>The woman, dress, position, dogs ... is perfect. But the woman''s face does not convey the spectacular serenity of Vermeer''s portraits. The background should have been a lot darker.<br/> <br/>This being said, I will mark this shot very high since the work and intention is unparalleled. But I do not love this picture since it is too much of a hybrid. Your work and talent is much superior to this shot.</td>', 'Very, very ambitious shot. Hard to mark though. I applaud your work, tenacity, humour, fearlessness, photo skills.Am wondering what Vermeer would think of it.Do you know the work of Ori Gerscht? Since I have an inkling of the photographer I can formulate several problems that I have with this picture: you wanted to tell too much and crowded your shot with too many props, the opposite of what Vermeer did. Hard to crop it but it might benefit from it. The screen looks a bit cheap and does not match the intention and the style of the foreground. Same for the chair, an almost Adirondack style as far from the subject as it could be. The window in the background should have been obstructed in favor of the central subject.The woman, dress, position, dogs ... is perfect. But the woman''s face does not convey the spectacular serenity of Vermeer''s portraits. The background should have been a lot darker. This being said, I will mark this shot very high since the work and intention is unparalleled. But I do not love this picture since it is too much of a hybrid. Your work and talent is much superior to this shot.', '2011-10-19 23:08:38.000000', NULL, 1),
